flowchart TB
  accTitle: How an effect of the light show plays
  accDescr: A moment with an effect saves the lights and pauses the detection if it runs, unless the moment is the daily goal or a new best session average. Its actions start the effect, which plays for the effect duration. If a training session ends meanwhile, the effect ends at once and the detection stays off. A new session lets the effect play to its end. Then the lights are restored and a paused detection starts again.
  MOMENT["A moment with an effect"] --> SAVE["Save the lights"]
  SAVE --> PAUSE{"Detection running,<br/>not the daily goal or a<br/>best session average?"}
  PAUSE -- "yes" --> STOP["Pause the detection"]
  PAUSE -- "no" --> ACTIONS["Your actions<br/>start the effect"]
  STOP --> ACTIONS
  ACTIONS --> PLAY{"Effect duration over,<br/>or the session ended?"}
  PLAY -- "duration over" --> RESTORE["Restore the lights"]
  PLAY -- "new session" --> REST["Play to the end"]
  REST --> RESTORE
  PLAY -- "session ended" --> ENDED["Lights back at once,<br/>detection stays off"]
  RESTORE --> RESUME["Start a paused<br/>detection again"]
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef warn fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
  class RESUME done
  class ENDED warn
